## Contract Address Publication

Gene will publish the contract address **as soon as the token is created — during the protection window, not after it.**

This is deliberate. The window only produces a fair start if everyone has the address *before* trading opens. Publishing it late would leave the audience arriving after the open while automated systems, which monitor the chain rather than Gene's feed, were ready the whole time. That would hand back the exact advantage the window exists to remove.

The consequence is that the address is public while the 99% fee is still active. But the CA announcement will be timed as best as possible so once participants see it, paste it in their terminals, and buy that protection window will most likely have just ended.

**Do not trade during that period.** If you use any major terminals, they will state the fee at the top so you can clearly see once the 30s window has ended.

